{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetKhYnkvr2MCcP8XaBxb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Summary of Repository Findings:**\n\nFrom my exploration, I found:\n\n1. **Shipment Model** (`Shipment.kt:9-27`): Defines `Shipment` with status enum having `CREATED`, `CONFIRMED`, `CANCELLED`\n2. **ShipmentController** (`ShipmentController.kt:20-56`): Currently has `@PostMapping` (create), `@GetMapping(\"/{shipmentId}\")` (get by id), and `@GetMapping` (list)\n3. **InMemoryShipmentRepository** (`ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27`): Provides `save()`, `existsById()`, `findById()`, `findAll()`, `clear()`\n4. **Error Handling Pattern** (`ApiExceptions.kt:11-30`): Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses (`ResourceNotFoundException`, `ConflictException`)\n5. **Error Codes** (`ApiError.kt:31-37`): Enum with `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`, `ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS`, `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`, `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS`, `VALIDATION_FAILED`\n6. **Test Pattern** (`ShipmentControllerTest.kt:20-84`): MockMvc with jsonPath assertions on error codes (e.g., `$.error.code`)\n\n**Conventions This Repository Has:**\n\n- Exceptions define both HTTP status and error code; `GlobalExceptionHandler` converts them to the unified error envelope\n- POST endpoints return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(...)`\n- Tests verify response bodies, including `$.error.code` assertions, not just status codes\n- Repository state is reset via `@BeforeEach` in tests\n- The skill guidance emphasizes: verify state changes with a **separate GET request**, not just the mutating call's response\n\n**Affected Files & Why:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Must add a new error code (e.g., `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED`) for the 409 case; the ticket names this error but no existing code matches it\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Must add the `/confirm` endpoint with the logic for all four cases\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Must add tests covering confirm, repeat confirm (idempotent), cancelled rejection, and not-found rejection\n\n**Risks:**\n\n- Adding a new error code changes the `ErrorCode` enum; if I get the name wrong, compilation breaks\n- Idempotency logic must be correct: second confirm of already-CONFIRMED shipment must succeed with 200, not 409\n- Forgetting to verify persistence via a second GET request (per skill guidance)\n\n**Open Questions:**\n\n- The ticket says \"Error responses are consistent\" but does not specify the error code for the cancelled case. Based on the existing pattern (specific codes like `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS`), I will add `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` as a new code.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed Change:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` to the `ErrorCode` enum (line 36, before `VALIDATION_FAILED`)\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>\n   ```\n   Logic:\n   - Fetch shipment by id; throw `ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND)` if absent\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throw `ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANCELLED)`\n   - If status is `CONFIRMED`, do nothing (idempotent)\n   - If status is `CREATED`, update to `CONFIRMED`\n   - Save and return the shipment with 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and persists it` — POST to confirm, verify 200, assert body has CONFIRMED status, then GET and assert persisted as CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm is idempotent for already confirmed shipment` — POST to confirm twice, assert second call returns 200 with CONFIRMED, GET and verify no side effects\n   - `confirms a cancelled shipment is rejected with 409` — Create a cancelled shipment in repo directly, POST to confirm, assert 409, `$.error.code` = SHIPMENT_CANCELLED, GET and assert still CANCELLED (unchanged)\n   - `confirms an unknown shipment is rejected with 404` — POST to confirm non-existent id, assert 404, `$.error.code` = SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternatives Rejected:**\n\n1. **Add a service layer** — The existing codebase does not have one; the controller directly manages state. Adding one would violate the \"preserve existing architecture\" constraint.\n2. **Reuse existing error codes** — Could use `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` for the cancelled case, but it would be semantically incorrect and confusing; `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` is more precise and follows the pattern.\n3. **Return 400 for cancelled shipments** — The ticket explicitly requires 409 (conflict), which is semantically correct: the request conflicts with the current state.\n\n**Data and Error Flow:**\n\n- **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED)**: GET by id → verify CREATED → POST confirm → repository.save() → return 200 with CONFIRMED → GET by id → verify persisted as CONFIRMED\n- **Idempotent path (already CONFIRMED)**: GET by id → verify CONFIRMED → POST confirm → no change → repository.save() → return 200 with CONFIRMED (no diff)\n- **Cancelled rejection**: POST confirm → ResourceNotFoundException → 404 → GlobalExceptionHandler → `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": []}}`; or POST confirm on CANCELLED → ConflictException → 409 → GlobalExceptionHandler → `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"SHIPMENT_CANCELLED\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": []}}`\n- **Not found rejection**: POST confirm on missing id → ResourceNotFoundException → 404 → GlobalExceptionHandler → error envelope\n\n**Test Strategy:**\n\n1. **Happy path test** — Create a shipment, confirm it, assert 200 and body has CONFIRMED, then GET and assert persisted\n2. **Idempotent test** — Create shipment, confirm twice, second call returns 200 with CONFIRMED, verify no unintended mutations\n3. **Cancelled rejection test** — Insert a CANCELLED shipment directly into repo, attempt confirm, assert 409 and error.code = SHIPMENT_CANCELLED, then GET and verify still CANCELLED\n4. **Not found rejection test** — Confirm a non-existent id, assert 404 and error.code = SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. First, add the new error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1195,"cache_read_input_tokens":18359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1195},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f367e145-8b2a-4a98-8d7f-dd1384f85bfe","uuid":"60e91e70-189b-4573-8e1b-d01c0d3829c1","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:16:52.030Z","request_id":"req_011CetKhYAnjJqMSh2whKP8v"}
